msgstr "sugár: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/acos.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>acos</code>"
msgstr "Utasítás <code>acos</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/acos.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>acos ( value );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>acos ( érték );<n/>"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/acos.txt:5 ../E/asin.txt:5 ../E/atan.txt:5 ../E/ceil.txt:6
#: ../E/floor.txt:6 ../E/round.txt:6 ../E/sqrt.txt:5 ../E/trunc.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "value: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>"
msgstr "érték: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/acos.txt:6 ../E/asin.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Number between -1 and 1 (including both)."
msgstr "Szám -1 és 1 között (beleértve a szélső értékeket is)."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/acos.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arcus cosine (in degrees) of the value."
msgstr "Az érték arkusz koszinusza (fokban)."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/acos.txt:12 ../E/asin.txt:12 ../E/atan.txt:12 ../E/atan2.txt:17
#: ../E/cos.txt:12 ../E/pow.txt:15 ../E/rand.txt:9 ../E/sin.txt:12
#: ../E/sqrt.txt:12 ../E/tan.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|expr>expressions</a>."
msgstr "<a cbot>Programozás</a>, <a cbot|type>típusok</a> és <a cbot|expr>kifejezések</a>."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/aim.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>aim ( y, x );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>aim ( y, x );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/aim.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "This instruction sets the vertical and the horizontal angle of the cannon. The following robots are equipped with a cannon: "
msgstr "Ez az utasítás beállítja az ágyú függőleges és vízszintes szögét. A következő robotok vannak ágyúval felszerelve: "

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/aim.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "When controlling the robot through programming, the gun can be also turned left or right by turning the whole robot with the instruction <code><a cbot|turn>turn</a></code>."
msgstr "A robot programozott irányítása során az ágyú balra vagy jobbra is elforgatható az egész robot elfordításával a <code><a cbot|turn>turn</a></code> utasítással."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/aim.txt:12 ../E/atan2.txt:7 ../E/pow.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "y: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>"
msgstr "y: <code><a cbot|float>lebegőpontos szám</a></code>"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/aim.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "x: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code> (default value: <code>0</code>)"
msgstr "x: <code><a cbot|float>lebegőpontos szám</a></code> (alapértelmezett érték: <code>0</code>)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/aim.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Angle in degrees of the gun relative to the robot. A positive value orients the gun to the right. The angle must range from <code>-40</code> to <code>+40</code> degrees for all shooters."
msgstr "Az ágyú szöge fokban, a robothoz viszonyítva. A pozitív érték jobbra fordítja az ágyút. A szögnek minden lövő esetén <code>-40</code> és <code>+40</code> fok között kell lennie."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/asin.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>asin</code>"
msgstr "Utasítás: <code>asin</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/asin.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>asin ( value );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>asin ( érték );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/asin.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arcus sine (in degrees) of the value."
msgstr "Az érték arkusz szinusza (fokban)."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/atan.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>atan</code>"
msgstr "Utasítás: <code>atan</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/atan.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>atan ( value );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>atan ( érték );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/atan.txt:6 ../E/atan2.txt:8 ../E/atan2.txt:11 ../E/ceil.txt:7
#: ../E/floor.txt:7 ../E/round.txt:7 ../E/trunc.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Number."
msgstr "Szám."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/atan.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arcus tangent (in degrees) of the value."
msgstr "Az érték arkusz tangense (fokban)."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/atan2.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>atan2</code>"
msgstr "Utasítás: <code>atan2</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/atan2.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>atan2 ( y, x );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>atan2 ( y, x );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/atan2.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "The purpose of using two arguments instead of one is to gather information on the signs of the inputs in order to return the appropriate quadrant of the computed angle, which is not possible for the single-argument <c/><a cbot|atan>atan();</a><n/> function. For example, consider a point <code>(-1, -1)</code>: <c/>atan(-1/-1);<n/> is <code>45.00</code> degrees, whereas <c/>atan2(-1, -1);<n/> is <code>-135.00</code> degrees, which is obviously more correct in this case."
msgstr "A két paraméter használatának célja az értékek előjeléből való következtetés, hogy a számított szög megfelelő negyedét vissza tudja adni – amit az egy paraméteres <c/><a cbot|atan>atan();</a><n/> függvény nem tud. Például a <code>(-1, -1)</code> pontnál: <c/>atan(-1/-1);<n/> eredménye <code>45.00</code> fok, míg <c/>atan2(-1, -1);<n/> eredménye <code>-135.00</code> fok, ami ebben az esetben nyilvánvalóan helyesebb."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/atan2.txt:10 ../E/pow.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "x: <code><a cbot|float>float</a></code>"
msgstr "x: <code><a cbot|float>lebegőpontos szám</a></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/atan2.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arcus tangent (in degrees) of <code>y/x</code>."
msgstr "A <code>y/x</code> hányados arkusz tangense (fokban)."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/build.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>build</code>"
msgstr "Utasítás <code>build</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/build.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <a cbot|object>object</a> item = <a cbot|radar>radar</a>(<a object|titan>Titanium</a>);\n"
" <a cbot|goto>goto</a>(item.position);\n"
" build(<a object|factory>BotFactory</a>);"
msgstr ""
" <a cbot|object>object</a> item = <a cbot|radar>radar</a>(<a object|titan>Titanium</a>);\n"
" <a cbot|goto>goto</a>(item.position);\n"
" build(<a object|factory>BotFactory</a>);"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/build.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>build ( cat );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>build ( cat );<n/>"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/build.txt:17 ../E/buildingenabled.txt:16 ../E/canbuild.txt:16
#: ../E/detect.txt:11 ../E/factory.txt:7 ../E/radar.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "cat: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>"
msgstr "cat: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/build.txt:18 ../E/buildingenabled.txt:17 ../E/canbuild.txt:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a cbot|category>Category</a> of a building."
msgstr "Egy épület <a cbot|category>kategóriája</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/build.txt:21
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally an error stops the program. You can prevent the program from stopping on errors by using the <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code> instruction. A value different from zero if an error occurred is then returned by <code>build()</code>.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>Successfully built\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>Impossible to build (for example, the nearest titanium cube is too far away or the specified building is not available in the mission)"
msgstr ""
"Hiba esetén a program általában leáll. Ezt elkerülheted azzal, ha használod az <code><a cbot|errmode>errmode</a>(0)</code> utasítást. A <code>build()</code> ekkor egy nullától különböző értéket ad vissza, ha hiba történt.\n"
"<code>== 0 </code>Az építés sikeres volt\n"
"<code>!= 0 </code>Nem lehet építeni (például a legközelebbi titánkocka túl messze van, vagy az adott épület nem érhető el az adott küldetésben)"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/buildingenabled.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>buildingenabled</code>"
msgstr "Utasítás <code>buildingenabled</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/buildingenabled.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is similar to the <c/><a cbot|canbuild>canbuild();</a><n/> instruction. However, it does not check if a required research has been done."
msgstr "Hasonló a <c/><a cbot|canbuild>canbuild();</a><n/> utasításhoz, de nem ellenőrzi, hogy az adott kutatás már el lett-e végezve."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/buildingenabled.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <a cbot|if>if</a> (buildingenabled(<a object|factory>BotFactory</a>))\n"
" {\n"
" \tbuild(<a object|factory>BotFactory</a>);\n"
" }"
msgstr ""
" <a cbot|if>if</a> (buildingenabled(<a object|factory>BotFactory</a>))\n"
" {\n"
" \tbuild(<a object|factory>BotFactory</a>);\n"
" }"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/buildingenabled.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>buildingenabled ( cat );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>buildingenabled ( cat );<n/>"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/buildingenabled.txt:19 ../E/canbuild.txt:19 ../E/canresearch.txt:10
#: ../E/detect.txt:23 ../E/isbusy.txt:10 ../E/researched.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Return value: <code><a cbot|bool>bool</a></code>"
msgstr "Visszatérési érték: <code><a cbot|bool>bool</a></code>"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/destroy.txt:7 ../E/factory.txt:13 ../E/isbusy.txt:7
#: ../E/research.txt:10 ../E/takeoff.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a cbot|object>object</a>"
msgstr "<a cbot|object>object</a>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/isbusy.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Any building which can take some action (e.g. <a cbot|convert>Converter</a>)."
msgstr "Bármely épület, amely képes valamilyen műveletet végezni (pl. <a cbot|convert>átalakító</a>)."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/isbusy.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><format const>true</format></code> if the object is doing something (e.g. converting)\n"
"<code><format const>false</format></code> if the object is not doing anything"
msgstr ""
"<code><format const>true</format></code>, ha az objektum éppen valamit csinál (pl. átalakít)\n"
"<code><format const>false</format></code>, ha az objektum nem végez semmilyen műveletet"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/canbuild.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>canbuild</code>"
msgstr "Utasítás <code>canbuild</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/canbuild.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "It helps to prevent errors in programs using the <c/><a cbot|build>build();</a><n/> instruction. Here is an example:"
msgstr "Segít megelőzni a hibákat azokban a programokban, amelyek a <c/><a cbot|build>build();</a><n/> utasítást használják. Itt egy példa:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/canbuild.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <a cbot|if>if</a> (canbuild(<a object|factory>BotFactory</a>))\n"
" {\n"
" \tbuild(<a object|factory>BotFactory</a>);\n"
" }"
msgstr ""
" <a cbot|if>if</a> (canbuild(<a object|factory>BotFactory</a>))\n"
" {\n"
" \tbuild(<a object|factory>BotFactory</a>);\n"
" }"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/canbuild.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>canbuild ( cat );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>canbuild ( cat );<n/>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/buildingenabled.txt:20 ../E/canbuild.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>true</code> if the building can be built, <code>false</code> otherwise."
msgstr "<code>true</code>, ha az épület felépíthető, <code>false</code>, ha nem."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/canresearch.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>canresearch</code>"
msgstr "Utasítás: <code>canresearch</code>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/canresearch.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>canresearch ( research );<n/>"
msgstr "<c/>canresearch ( research );<n/>"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/canresearch.txt:7 ../E/researched.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "research: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>"
msgstr "kutatás: <code><a cbot|int>int</a></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/canresearch.txt:8 ../E/research.txt:8 ../E/researched.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a cbot|researches>Research name</a>."
msgstr "<a cbot|researches>Kutatás neve</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/canresearch.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<format const>true</format> if the research can be done (even if it is already done, to check that, use the <a cbot|researched>researched</a> instruction)\n"
"<format const>false</format> if the research cannot be done"
msgstr ""
"<format const>true</format>, ha a kutatás elvégezhető (még akkor is, ha már el van végezve – ennek ellenőrzéséhez használd a <a cbot|researched>researched</a> utasítást)\n"
"<format const>false</format>, ha a kutatás nem végezhető el"

