#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classes can be only <a cbot|public>public</a>. This means that they can be used by all bots in a mission."
msgstr "Az osztályok csak <a cbot|public>nyilvános</a> lehetnek. Ez azt jelenti, hogy minden robot használhatja őket egy küldetés során."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/class.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Class Members"
msgstr "Osztálytagok"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Class members are fields (<a cbot|var>variables</a>) and methods (<a cbot|function>functions</a>)."
msgstr "Az osztálytagok mezők (<a cbot|var>változók</a>) és metódusok (<a cbot|function>függvények</a>)."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, the following class dubbed <code>MyClass</code> contains 4 fields (<code>a</code>, <code>b</code>, <code>x</code> and <code>s</code>) and one method (<code>MyFunction</code>)."
msgstr "Például az alábbi <code>MyClass</code> nevű osztály 4 mezőt (<code>a</code>, <code>b</code>, <code>x</code> és <code>s</code>) és egy metódust (<code>MyFunction</code>) tartalmaz."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/class.txt:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"public class MyClass\n"
"{\n"
"\tint     a, b;\n"
"\tfloat   x = 3.33;\n"
"\tstring  s = \"hello\";\n"
"\tfloat   MyFunction(float value)\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\treturn (value * x) - 1;\n"
"\t}\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"public class MyClass\n"
"{\n"
"\tint     a, b;\n"
"\tfloat   x = 3.33;\n"
"\tstring  s = \"hello\";\n"
"\tfloat   MyFunction(float value)\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\treturn (value * x) - 1;\n"
"\t}\n"
"}"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/class.txt:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "Member Initialization"
msgstr "Tagok inicializálása"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example:<c/>"
msgstr "Példa:<c/>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/class.txt:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"public class MyClass\n"
"{\n"
"\tint  a, b;\n"
"\tvoid MyClass()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\ta = 2;  b = 3;\n"
"\t}\n"
"\tvoid MyClass(int a, int b)\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tthis.a = a;  this.b = b;\n"
"\t}\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"public class MyClass\n"
"{\n"
"\tint  a, b;\n"
"\tvoid MyClass()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\ta = 2;  b = 3;\n"
"\t}\n"
"\tvoid MyClass(int a, int b)\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tthis.a = a;  this.b = b;\n"
"\t}\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "As the names of the parameters of the second constructor are the same as the names of the two members <code>a</code> and <code>b</code>, we must use the <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code> <a cbot|pointer>reference</a> to avoid confusion with the parameters' names."
msgstr "Mivel a második konstruktor paramétereinek nevei megegyeznek a két tag, a <code>a</code> és <code>b</code> neveivel, használni kell a <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code> <a cbot|pointer>referenciát</a>, hogy elkerüljük a paraméterek nevei miatti összezavarodást."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/class.txt:78
#, no-wrap
msgid "Object Creation"
msgstr "Objektum létrehozása"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:79
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can create objects of type <code>YourClass</code> using the <code><a cbot|new>new</a></code> keyword. Example:"
msgstr "Objektumokat hozhatsz létre a <code>YourClass</code> típusból a <code><a cbot|new>new</a></code> kulcsszó segítségével. Példa:"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/class.txt:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "Object Destruction"
msgstr "Objektum megsemmisítése"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/class.txt:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "Passing Objects to Functions"
msgstr "Objektumok átadása függvényeknek"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:115
#, no-wrap
msgid "Objects in CBOT are passed by <a cbot|pointer>reference</a>. This means that when an object is passed to a <a cbot|function>function</a>, the function receives a copy of a pointer to the instance, not a copy of the object, so any modifications on the object will be visible outside of the function."
msgstr "A CBOT-ban az objektumokat <a cbot|pointer>referenciával</a> adjuk át. Ez azt jelenti, hogy amikor egy objektumot átadunk egy <a cbot|function>függvénynek</a>, a függvény az objektum mutatójának másolatát kapja meg, nem az objektum másolatát, tehát az objektum módosításai kívülről is láthatók lesznek."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/class.txt:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inheritance"
msgstr "Öröklődés"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "A class can inherit public and protected members of another class by using the <code><a cbot|extends>extends</a></code> keyword."
msgstr "Egy osztály örökölhet más osztályok nyilvános és védett tagjait a <code><a cbot|extends>extends</a></code> kulcsszó használatával."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "This keyword allows you to create a class definition by using the following syntax:"
msgstr "Ez a kulcsszó lehetővé teszi osztálydefiníció létrehozását az alábbi szintaxis segítségével:"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/class.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "All Classes Are Public"
msgstr "Minden osztály nyilvános"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/class.txt:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "Class Members Modifiers"
msgstr "Osztálytagok módosítói"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/class.txt:75
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code>"
msgstr "A <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code> használata"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/class.txt:81
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tMyClass object1();       // Call default constructor (without parameters)\n"
"\tMyClass object2(4, 5);   // Call constructor with two int parameters\n"
"\tMyClass object3;         // No constructor called, object3 == null\n"
"\tobject3 = new MyClass(); // We call constructor now, object3 != null\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tMyClass object1();       // Call default constructor (without parameters)\n"
"\tMyClass object2(4, 5);   // Call constructor with two int parameters\n"
"\tMyClass object3;         // No constructor called, object3 == null\n"
"\tobject3 = new MyClass(); // We call constructor now, object3 != null\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also define a destructor. This must be a <code><a cbot|void>void</a></code> fonction without parameters, which has the same name as the class but prefixed with the <code>~</code> character. The destructor is called automatically as soon as the class instance is no more referenced by anyone. Example:"
msgstr "Desztruktort is definiálhatsz. Ennek egy <code><a cbot|void>void</a></code> típusú függvénynek kell lennie, paraméterek nélkül, amelynek ugyanaz a neve, mint az osztálynak, de a <code>~</code> karakterrel kezdődik. A desztruktor automatikusan meghívódik, amint az osztály példányára már nincs hivatkozás. Példa:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/class.txt:93
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"public class MyClass\n"
"{\n"
"\tstatic private int counter = 0; // instance counter\n"
"\tvoid  MyClass( )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tcounter++;  // one instance more\n"
"\t}\n"
"\tvoid ~MyClass( )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tcounter--;  // one instance less\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\t                   // counter == 0\n"
"\tMyClass item1( );  // counter == 1\n"
"\tMyClass item2( );  // counter == 2\n"
"\titem1 = null;      // counter == 1\n"
"}\n"
"// counter == 0"
msgstr ""
"public class MyClass\n"
"{\n"
"\tstatic private int counter = 0; // instance counter\n"
"\tvoid  MyClass( )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tcounter++;  // one instance more\n"
"\t}\n"
"\tvoid ~MyClass( )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tcounter--;  // one instance less\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\t                   // counter == 0\n"
"\tMyClass item1( );  // counter == 1\n"
"\tMyClass item2( );  // counter == 2\n"
"\titem1 = null;      // counter == 1\n"
"}\n"
"// counter == 0"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/class.txt:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "Accessing Class Members"
msgstr "Osztálytagok elérése"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "Class members can be accessed outside of the class definition by using the <code>.</code> operator. Example:"
msgstr "Az osztálytagok a <code>.</code> operátorral elérhetők az osztály definícióján kívül. Példa:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "Class members are <a cbot|public>public</a> by default, which means that they are accessible outside of the class definition. They can also be declared as <code><a cbot|private>private</a></code> or <code><a cbot|protected>protected</a></code>. Such members can only be accessed inside of the class definition."
msgstr "Az osztálytagok alapértelmezés szerint <a cbot|public>public</a> láthatóságúak, ami azt jelenti, hogy elérhetők az osztály definícióján kívül is. Ezen kívül deklarálhatók <code><a cbot|private>private</a></code> vagy <code><a cbot|protected>protected</a></code> láthatóságúak is. Az ilyen tagokat csak az osztály definícióján belül lehet elérni."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fields and methods can also be declared as <code><a cbot|static>static</a></code>. Methods can be additionaly declared as <code><a cbot|synchro>synchronized</a></code>."
msgstr "A mezők és metódusok <code><a cbot|static>static</a></code> típusúak is lehetnek. A metódusok továbbiakban deklarálhatók <code><a cbot|synchro>synchronized</a></code> kulcsszóval is."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "Another way of initiliazing fields is by defining a constructor which is a special method having the same name as the class. This method will be called automatically at <a cbot|new>creation</a> time of a class instance. Constructors can be <a cbot|function>overloaded</a>."
msgstr "A mezők inicializálásának egy másik módja az, hogy definiálsz egy konstruktort, amely egy speciális metódus, és ugyanaz a neve, mint az osztálynak. Ez a metódus automatikusan meghívódik egy osztálypéldány <a cbot|new>létrehozásakor</a>. A konstruktorok <a cbot|function>túlterhelhetők</a>."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/class.txt:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"public class MyClass\n"
"{\n"
"\tint myField = 0;\n"
"\tint MyFunction()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\treturn myField * 2;\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tMyClass myObject();\n"
"\tmyObject.myField = 10;\n"
"\tmessage(myObject.MyFunction()); // 20\n"
"\tMyClass mySecondObject();\n"
"\tmySecondObject.myField = myObject.myField - 2;\n"
"\tmessage(mySecondObject.MyFunction()); // 16\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"public class MyClass\n"
"{\n"
"\tint myField = 0;\n"
"\tint MyFunction()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\treturn myField * 2;\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tMyClass myObject();\n"
"\tmyObject.myField = 10;\n"
"\tmessage(myObject.MyFunction()); // 20\n"
"\tMyClass mySecondObject();\n"
"\tmySecondObject.myField = myObject.myField - 2;\n"
"\tmessage(mySecondObject.MyFunction()); // 16\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:121
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|public>public</a></code>, <code><a cbot|private>private</a></code>, <code><a cbot|protected>protected</a></code>, <code><a cbot|static>static</a></code>, <code><a cbot|synchro>synchronized</a></code>, <code><a cbot|new>new</a></code>, <code><a cbot|pointer>reference</a></code>, <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code>, <code><a cbot|super>super</a></code>, <code><a cbot|extends>extends</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|public>public</a></code>, <code><a cbot|private>private</a></code>, <code><a cbot|protected>protected</a></code>, <code><a cbot|static>static</a></code>, <code><a cbot|synchro>synchronized</a></code>, <code><a cbot|new>new</a></code>, <code><a cbot|pointer>reference</a></code>, <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code>, <code><a cbot|super>super</a></code>, <code><a cbot|extends>extends</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/protected.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keyword <code>protected</code>"
msgstr "A(z) <code>protected</code> kulcsszó"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/protected.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is an access modifier for <a cbot|class>class</a> members. Protected class members can be accessed in a child class, but they can't be accessed outside of classes definitions being part of the same inheritance tree (see the <code><a cbot|extends>extends</a></code> keyword)."
msgstr "Ez egy hozzáférési módosító az <a cbot|class>osztály</a> tagjaihoz. A védett osztálytagokat elérhetjük egy gyermekosztályban, de nem érhetők el az osztályok definícióin kívül, amelyek ugyanazon öröklési fa részét képezik (lásd a <code><a cbot|extends>extends</a></code> kulcsszót)."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/protected.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"public class Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tprotected int field = 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public class Child extends Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid Print()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(field);\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tChild child();\n"
"\tchild.Print(); // 0\n"
"\t//child.field = 1; // Error!\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"public class Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tprotected int field = 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public class Child extends Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid Print()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(field);\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tChild child();\n"
"\tchild.Print(); // 0\n"
"\t//child.field = 1; // Error!\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/private.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is an access modifier for <a cbot|class>class</a> members. Private members are not accessible outside of the class definition."
msgstr "Ez egy hozzáférési módosító a <a cbot|class>osztály</a> tagjaihoz. A privát tagok nem elérhetők az osztály definícióján kívül."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/private.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|public>public</a></code>, <code><a cbot|protected>protected</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|public>public</a></code>, <code><a cbot|protected>protected</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/public.txt:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>public</code> is also an access modifier for <a cbot|class>class</a> members, which is the default one. Public members can be accessed from outside of the class definition."
msgstr "<code>public</code> szintén hozzáférési módosító az <a cbot|class>osztály</a> tagjaihoz, és ez az alapértelmezett. A nyilvános tagok elérhetők az osztály definícióján kívülről."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/public.txt:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|private>private</a></code>, <code><a cbot|protected>protected</a></code>, <code><a cbot|function>functions</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|private>private</a></code>, <code><a cbot|protected>protected</a></code>, <code><a cbot|function>functions</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/protected.txt:27
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|public>public</a></code>, <code><a cbot|private>private</a></code>, <code><a cbot|extends>extends</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|public>public</a></code>, <code><a cbot|private>private</a></code>, <code><a cbot|extends>extends</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/super.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keyword <code>super</code>"
msgstr "Kulcsszó <code>super</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/super.txt:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/this.txt:53
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|super>super</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|super>super</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/extends.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keyword <code>extends</code>"
msgstr "Kulcsszó <code>extends</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/extends.txt:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inherited Members"
msgstr "Örökölt tagok"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/extends.txt:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only <code><a cbot|public>public</a></code> and <code><a cbot|protected>protected</a></code> members are inherited. <code><a cbot|private>private</a></code> members are directly inaccessible even for a child, although they can be accessed indirectly through inherited methods."
msgstr "Csak a <code><a cbot|public>nyilvános</a></code> és <code><a cbot|protected>védett</a></code> tagok öröklődnek. A <code><a cbot|private>privát</a></code> tagok közvetlenül nem elérhetők még gyermek osztályok számára sem, bár hozzáférhetők lehetnek közvetve az örökölt metódusokon keresztül."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/extends.txt:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "Constructors and destructors are not inherited, however, they can be overriden."
msgstr "A konstruktorok és destruktorok nem öröklődnek, azonban felülírhatók."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/extends.txt:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "Method Overriding"
msgstr "Metódus felülírás"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/extends.txt:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inherited methods can be overriden (redefined) in the child class definition. Example:"
msgstr "Az örökölt metódusokat felülírhatjuk (újradefiniálhatjuk) a gyermekosztály definíciójában. Példa:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/extends.txt:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"public class Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid foo()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"foo\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public class Child extends Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid foo()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"bar\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tChild child();\n"
"\tchild.foo(); // Will show \"bar\"\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"public class Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid foo()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"foo\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public class Child extends Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid foo()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"bar\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tChild child();\n"
"\tchild.foo(); // Will show \"bar\"\n"
"}"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/extends.txt:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "Polymorphism"
msgstr "Polimorfizmus"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/extends.txt:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code><a cbot|pointer>Reference</a></code> of type Parent can point to an object of type Child. However, such a pointer can't be used to access a child member. In order to access a child member, it must be assured that the Parent reference really points to a Child object. If that's the case, it can be safely copied to a pointer of type Child, which has access to the child members."
msgstr "<code><a cbot|pointer>Referencia</a></code> a Parent típusú objektumból egy Child típusú objektumra mutathat. Azonban egy ilyen pointer nem használható gyermek tag elérésére. Ahhoz, hogy hozzáférhessünk egy gyermek tagnak, biztosítani kell, hogy a Parent referencia valóban egy Child objektumra mutasson. Ha ez így van, biztonságosan másolható egy Child típusú pointerre, amely hozzáfér a gyermek tagokhoz."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/extends.txt:67
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"public class Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid foo()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"foo\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public class Child extends Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid foo()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"bar\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"\tvoid bar()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"foo bar\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tParent people[2];\n"
"\tpeople[0] = new Parent();\n"
"\tpeople[1] = new Child();\n"
"\tfor (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i)\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tpeople[i].foo();\n"
"\t}\n"
"\t//people[1].bar(); // Error\n"
"\tChild child = people[1];\n"
"\tchild.bar(); // OK\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"public class Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid foo()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"foo\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public class Child extends Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid foo()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"bar\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"\tvoid bar()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"foo bar\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tParent people[2];\n"
"\tpeople[0] = new Parent();\n"
"\tpeople[1] = new Child();\n"
"\tfor (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i)\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tpeople[i].foo();\n"
"\t}\n"
"\t//people[1].bar(); // Error\n"
"\tChild child = people[1];\n"
"\tchild.bar(); // OK\n"
"}"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/extends.txt:102
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple Inheritance"
msgstr "Többszörös öröklődés"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/extends.txt:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "A child cannot have multiple parents, however, a parent can have many children."
msgstr "Egy gyermeknek nem lehet több szülő, azonban egy szülőnek sok gyermek is lehet."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/extends.txt:106
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|public>public</a></code>, <code><a cbot|private>private</a></code>, <code><a cbot|protected>protected</a></code>, <code><a cbot|new>new</a></code>, <code><a cbot|pointer>reference</a></code>, <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code>, <code><a cbot|super>super</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|class>class</a></code>, <code><a cbot|public>public</a></code>, <code><a cbot|private>private</a></code>, <code><a cbot|protected>protected</a></code>, <code><a cbot|new>new</a></code>, <code><a cbot|pointer>reference</a></code>, <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code>, <code><a cbot|super>super</a></code>\n"
"<a cbot>Programozás</a>, <a cbot|type>típusok</a> és <a cbot|category>kategóriák</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/super.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "This keyword is similar to <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code>, however, it grants access to methods from the parent class (see the <code><a cbot|extends>extends</a></code> keyword), which is especially useful for method overriding."
msgstr "Ez a kulcsszó hasonló a <code><a cbot|this>this</a></code> kulcsszóhoz, azonban hozzáférést biztosít a szülőosztály metódusaihoz (lásd az <code><a cbot|extends>extends</a></code> kulcsszót), ami különösen hasznos a metódus felülírásakor."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/super.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"public class Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tprotected int field;\n"
"\t\n"
"\tvoid Parent()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tfield = 0;\n"
"\t}\n"
"\t\n"
"\tvoid Print()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"Parent's field: \" + field);\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public class Child extends Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tprivate int childsField;\n"
"\t\n"
"\tvoid Child()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tsuper.Parent();\n"
"\t\tchildsField = field + 1;\n"
"\t}\n"
"\t\n"
"\tvoid Print()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tsuper.Print();\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"Child's field: \" + childsField);\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tChild child();\n"
"\tchild.Print(); // Will show both 0 and 1\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"public class Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tprotected int field;\n"
"\t\n"
"\tvoid Parent()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tfield = 0;\n"
"\t}\n"
"\t\n"
"\tvoid Print()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"Parent's field: \" + field);\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public class Child extends Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tprivate int childsField;\n"
"\t\n"
"\tvoid Child()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tsuper.Parent();\n"
"\t\tchildsField = field + 1;\n"
"\t}\n"
"\t\n"
"\tvoid Print()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tsuper.Print();\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"Child's field: \" + childsField);\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tChild child();\n"
"\tchild.Print(); // Will show both 0 and 1\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/extends.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "This keyword is used in a <code><a cbot|class>class</a></code> definition when we want the class to inherit members from another class. The class which is extended we usually call a parent or base, the extending class we call a child."
msgstr "Ez a kulcsszó egy <code><a cbot|class>class</a></code> definíciójában kerül használatra, amikor azt szeretnénk, hogy az osztály örökölje egy másik osztály tagjait. Az osztály, amelyet kiterjesztünk, általában szülőnek vagy alapnak nevezzük, a kiterjesztő osztályt pedig gyermeknek."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/extends.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"public class Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid foo()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"foo\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public class Child extends Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid bar()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"bar\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tChild child();\n"
"\tchild.foo(); // Will show \"foo\"\n"
"\tchild.bar(); // Will show \"bar\"\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"public class Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid foo()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"foo\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public class Child extends Parent\n"
"{\n"
"\tvoid bar()\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmessage(\"bar\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"extern void object::Test()\n"
"{\n"
"\tChild child();\n"
"\tchild.foo(); // Will show \"foo\"\n"
"\tchild.bar(); // Will show \"bar\"\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/extends.txt:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "A parent's method can be called inside an overriden method by using the <code><a cbot|super>super</a></code> keyword."
msgstr "Egy szülői metódus meghívható egy felülírt metódusban a <code><a cbot|super>super</a></code> kulcsszó használatával."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/class.txt:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "As shown in the previous example, the class members can be initialized in the class definition (<c/>int x = 3.33;<n/>)."
msgstr "Ahogy az előző példában látható, az osztály tagjai inicializálhatók az osztály definíciójában (<c/>int x = 3.33;<n/>)."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/open.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code>\"r\"</code> mode: open for reading.\n"
"<code>\"w\"</code> mode: open for writing.\n"
"<code>\"a\"</code> mode: open for appending."
msgstr ""
"<code>\"r\"</code> mód: megnyitás olvasásra.\n"
"<code>\"w\"</code> mód: megnyitás írásra.\n"
"<code>\"a\"</code> mód: megnyitás hozzáfűzésre."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/openfile.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "<c/>openfile();<n/> opens an text file in the files/ folder. This is not a method of the <code><a cbot|file>file</a></code> class but openfile returns a <a cbot|pointer>reference</a> to a new instance of the file class. You must supply two parameters, the filename and the opening mode."
msgstr "<c/>openfile();<n/> egy szöveges fájlt nyit meg a files/ mappában. Ez nem a <code><a cbot|file>file</a></code> osztály egy metódusa, hanem az openfile egy <a cbot|pointer>referenciát</a> ad vissza az új fájl osztálypéldányhoz. Két paramétert kell megadni: a fájlnevet és a megnyitási módot."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/openfile.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code>\"r\"</code> mode: open for reading.\n"
"<code>\"w\"</code> mode: open for writing.\n"
"<code>\"w\"</code> mode: open for appending."
msgstr ""
"<code>\"r\"</code> mód: megnyitás olvasásra.\n"
"<code>\"w\"</code> mód: megnyitás írásra.\n"
"<code>\"w\"</code> mód: megnyitás hozzáfűzésre."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nothing but a name can be changed in the main function. The keyword <code><a cbot|extern>extern</a></code> distinguishes the main function from others."
msgstr "A main függvényben csak egy név változtatható. Az <code><a cbot|extern>extern</a></code> kulcsszó megkülönbözteti a main függvényt a többi függvénytől."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/function.txt:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "Public Functions"
msgstr "Nyilvános függvények"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/function.txt:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default Parameters"
msgstr "Alapértelmezett paraméterek"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "Last function parameters can have default values that can be omitted when calling."
msgstr "A függvény utolsó paramétereinek alapértelmezett értékei lehetnek, amelyek kihagyhatók a híváskor."

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/function.txt:132
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"float Add(float a = 0.0, float b = 0.0)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn a + b;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"// Somewhere in the main program...\n"
"Add(); // Will return 0.0\n"
"Add(2.0); // Will return 2.0\n"
"Add(2.0, 3.0); // Will return 5.0\n"
"// ..."
msgstr ""
"float Add(float a = 0.0, float b = 0.0)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn a + b;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"// Somewhere in the main program...\n"
"Add(); // Will return 0.0\n"
"Add(2.0); // Will return 2.0\n"
"Add(2.0, 3.0); // Will return 5.0\n"
"// ..."

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/function.txt:144
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default Parameters and Overloading"
msgstr "Alapértelmezett paraméterek és túlterhelés"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "Functions with default parameters still can be overloaded, one must only ensure that function calls are not ambiguous. For example, consider the following code:"
msgstr "Az alapértelmezett paraméterekkel rendelkező függvényeket továbbra is túlterhelhetjük, csak biztosítani kell, hogy a függvényhívások ne legyenek kétértelműek. Például, vegyük a következő kódot:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../E/function.txt:147
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"float Add(float a = 0.0, float b = 0.0)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn a + b;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"string Add(string a = \"\", string b = \"\")\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn a + b;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"// Somewhere in the main program...\n"
"Add(); // Compilation error: ambiguous call\n"
"Add(\"\"); // Ok\n"
"Add(0.0); // Ok\n"
"// ..."
msgstr ""
"float Add(float a = 0.0, float b = 0.0)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn a + b;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"string Add(string a = \"\", string b = \"\")\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn a + b;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"// Somewhere in the main program...\n"
"Add(); // Compilation error: ambiguous call\n"
"Add(\"\"); // Ok\n"
"Add(0.0); // Ok\n"
"// ..."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/function.txt:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that in the above example overloading causes the first default parameter to be useless as caller needs to pass it anyway in order to distinguish the two functions."
msgstr "Ne feledd, hogy a fenti példában a túlterhelés miatt az első alapértelmezett paraméter haszontalanná válik, mivel a hívónak úgyis át kell adnia, hogy megkülönböztesse a két függvényt."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/category.txt:70
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<button 192/>   <code><a object|botbr>WheeledBuilder</a>         </code>Wheeled Builder\n"
"<button 193/>   <code><a object|botbc>TrackedBuilder</a>         </code>Tracked Builder\n"
"<button 194/>   <code><a object|botbj>WingedBuilder</a>          </code>Winged Builder\n"
"<button 195/>   <code><a object|botbs>LeggedBuilder</a>          </code>Legged Builder"
msgstr ""
"<button 192/>   <code><a object|botbr>WheeledBuilder</a>         </code>Wheeled Builder\n"
"<button 193/>   <code><a object|botbc>TrackedBuilder</a>         </code>Tracked Builder\n"
"<button 194/>   <code><a object|botbj>WingedBuilder</a>          </code>Winged Builder\n"
"<button 195/>   <code><a object|botbs>LeggedBuilder</a>          </code>Legged Builder"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/build.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "The instruction <c/>build();<n/> instructs the bot to build a building of a given <a cbot|category>category</a>."
msgstr "A <c/>build();<n/> utasítás arra utasítja a botot, hogy építsen egy adott <a cbot|category>kategóriájú</a> épületet."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/build.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a program that looks for the nearest <a object|titan>titanium cube</a>, approaches it, and builds a <a object|factory>bot factory</a>."
msgstr "Itt van egy program, amely a legközelebbi <a object|titan>titánium kockát</a> keresi, odamegy hozzá, és épít egy <a object|factory>bot gyárat</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/build.txt:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|canbuild>canbuild</a></code>, <code><a cbot|buildingenabled>buildingenabled</a></code>.\n"
